## Rule-suite bypasses

GitHub records every push that a ruleset would have refused but a bypass actor made (`rulesets/rule-suites`, result `bypass`).
A protected-path merge is a solo-mode bypass when only the `protected-paths` check failed and a PR comment starting
"Solo-mode bypass:" came first (WP0.1, Appendix B D2). A deploy-key push lists no actor and is identified from the
ledger commit (D1).

